{"id":"CVE-2012-0861","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2013-01-04T22:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T18:38:14.953Z","description":"The vds_installer in Red Hat Enterprise Virtualization Manager (RHEV-M) before 3.1, when adding a host, uses the -k curl parameter when downloading deployUtil.py and vds_bootstrap.py, which prevents SSL certificates from being validated and allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary Python code via a man-in-the-middle attack.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2012-1508.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2012:1508"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/56825","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"56825"},{"url":"http://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2012-1506.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2012:1506"},{"url":"http://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2012-1505.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2012:1505"},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/80544","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"enterprise-ssl-certificates-mitm(80544)"},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id?1027838","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1027838"}],"vendors":["curl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2012-6086","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2014-01-29T18:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T21:21:28.456Z","description":"libs/zbxmedia/eztexting.c in Zabbix 1.8.x before 1.8.18rc1, 2.0.x before 2.0.8rc1, and 2.1.x before 2.1.2 does not properly set the CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYHOST option for libcurl, which allows man-in-the-middle attackers to spoof SSL servers via an arbitrary valid certificate.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/57103","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"57103"},{"url":"https://support.zabbix.com/browse/ZBX-5924","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2013/01/03/1","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20130103 Re: CVE request: Curl insecure usage"}],"vendors":["curl"]}
